{"name":"Infinity and Beyond","hex":"#6e7e99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"infinity","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Endlessness, unlimitedness, absence of a beginning, end or limits to size.","A number that has an infinite numerical value that cannot be counted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infinity"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"beyond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Further away than.","On the far side of."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Farther along or away.","In addition; more."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beyond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buzz Lightyear","blocks":[{"text":"Buzz Lightyear is a fictional character in the Disney–Pixar Toy Story franchise. He is a superhero action figure from an in-universe media franchise. Buzz is recognizable by his lime green, purple, and white space suit. Originally intended as a one-man band toy named Tinny, he evolved into a space ranger action figure during the development of Toy Story, a decision made by director John Lasseter. He is named after American astronaut Buzz Aldrin, the second person to walk on the Moon. Buzz Lightyear is a recurring character in all of the Toy Story franchise's animated feature films, including spin-offs. In the Toy Story films, he is voiced by Tim Allen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Buzz_Lightyear_sculpture_of_Toy_Story_Hotel_Shanghai_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Buzz_Lightyear_sculpture_of_Toy_Story_Hotel_Shanghai_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzz_Lightyear","wikidata":"Q1986193"},{"title":"Infinity","blocks":[{"text":"Infinity is something which is boundless, limitless, or endless. It is denoted by ∞, called the infinity symbol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/SierpinskiTriangle.svg/330px-SierpinskiTriangle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infinity","wikidata":"Q205"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/13/Lunar_Larry_sketch.jpg/250px-Lunar_Larry_sketch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/13/Lunar_Larry_sketch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/13/Lunar_Larry_sketch.jpg/250px-Lunar_Larry_sketch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This sketch of Buzz Lightyear shows him in an early design iteration as Lunar Larry.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALunar_Larry_sketch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Tim_Allen_2012.jpg/500px-Tim_Allen_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Tim_Allen_2012.jpg/500px-Tim_Allen_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tim Allen is the voice of Buzz Lightyear in the Toy Story filmography.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATim_Allen_2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"ht